<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<section xml:id="welcome">
  <title>Welcome to CSAwesome</title>

  <introduction>
      <p>
        Welcome to CSAwesome2! This version of CSAwesome follows the College
        Board 2026+ revisions. CSAwesome is a College Board endorsed
        curriculum for AP Computer Science A, an introductory college-level
        computer programming course in Java. 
        </p>

    </introduction>

      <subsection xml:id="sisters">
      <title>Sisters Rise Up</title>
     <p>
       If you are a woman taking Advanced Placement Computer Science (CSP and/or CSA) and 
       identify as Black, Hispanic/Latina, and/or Native American you are eligible for a free 
       mentoring program run by Dr. Barbara Ericson at the University of Michigan. She created 
       the first version of this ebook and she and her PhD students have added new types of 
       practice problems such as the mixed-up code problems. Sisters Rise Up offers weekly 
       one-hour remote help sessions and monthly two hour special sessions.  Students who enroll 
       in the program and send in their score(s) on the AP exams before the end of August 
       receive a $100 gift card.  The help sessions are led by experienced undergraduate college 
       students.  Students can start the enrollment process by providing information for a 
       parent or guardian at <url href="https://tinyurl.com/55z7tyb9">
       https://tinyurl.com/55z7tyb9</url>.
      </p>

</subsection>

</section>